</ul>
<blockquote>
q
</blockquote>
</li>
</ul>
````

Blanks between sublist items make the sublist loose, not the list (pin).
````
- a

  - b

  - c
.
<ul>
<li>
a
<ul>
<li>
<p>b</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>c</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
````

A block quote right after the blank makes the list loose even if a sublist follows (pin).
````
- a

  > q
  - b
.
<ul>
<li>
<p>a</p>
<blockquote>
<p>q</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>
b
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
````

A paragraph line after a sublist is the sublist item's lazy text (pin).
````
- a

  - b
  para
.
<ul>
<li>
a
<ul>
<li>
b
para
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
````

In a tight list item, a paragraph inside a block quote renders without p tags, as djot.js.
````
-
  > q
.
<ul>
<li>
<blockquote>
q
</blockquote>
</li>
</ul>
````

The same inside a fenced div.
````
-
  ::: d
  q
  :::
.
<ul>
<li>
<div class="d">
q
</div>
</li>
</ul>
````

Two paragraphs in a block quote in a tight item.
````
-
  > q
  >
  > r
.
<ul>
<li>
<blockquote>
q
r
</blockquote>
</li>
</ul>
````

A nested loose list inside a quote in a tight item keeps its own p tags (pin).
````
-
  > - x
  >
  > - y
.
<ul>
<li>
<blockquote>
<ul>
<li>
<p>x</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>y</p>
</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
</li>
</ul>
````

A loose item's block quote keeps its p tags (pin).
````
- a

  > q
- b
.
<ul>
<li>
<p>a</p>
<blockquote>
<p>q</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li>
<p>b</p>
</li>
</ul>
````

A list item's lazy paragraph line and the item's end carry their source positions.
```` ap
- a

  b
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-4:0:8) tight=false style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-4:0:8)
      para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
        str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
      para (3:3:7-4:0:8)
        str (3:3:7-3:3:7) text="b"
````

A bare marker's item: offsets count the marker line's single byte.
```` ap
-
  content
- b
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-4:0:15) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-3:0:11)
      para (2:3:4-3:0:11)
        str (2:3:4-2:9:10) text="content"
    list_item (3:1:12-4:0:15)
      para (3:3:14-4:0:15)
        str (3:3:14-3:3:14) text="b"
````

An indented list: items end in the marker column of the next line.
```` ap
 - a
 - b
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:2:1-3:0:9) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:2:1-2:1:5)
      para (1:4:3-2:0:4)
        str (1:4:3-1:4:3) text="a"
    list_item (2:2:6-3:0:9)
      para (2:4:8-3:0:9)
        str (2:4:8-2:4:8) text="b"
````

A list ends where the next block's content starts.
```` ap
- a

para
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-3:1:5) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-3:0:4)
      para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
        str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
  para (3:1:5-4:0:9)
    str (3:1:5-3:4:8) text="para"
````

A nested list ends where the item's next block starts; its item ends in the marker column.
```` ap
- a

  - b

  para
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-6:0:18) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-6:0:18)
      para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
        str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
      bullet_list (3:3:7-5:3:14) tight=true style="-"
        list_item (3:3:7-5:2:13)
          para (3:5:9-4:0:10)
            str (3:5:9-3:5:9) text="b"
      para (5:3:14-6:0:18)
        str (5:3:14-5:6:17) text="para"
````

A block quote followed by a blank line ends with that line.
```` ap
> q

> r
.
doc
  block_quote (1:1:0-3:0:4)
    para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
      str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="q"
  block_quote (3:1:5-4:0:8)
    para (3:3:7-4:0:8)
      str (3:3:7-3:3:7) text="r"
````

A block quote followed directly by a list ends where the list starts.
```` ap
> q
- a
.
doc
  block_quote (1:1:0-2:1:4)
    para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
      str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="q"
  bullet_list (2:1:4-3:0:7) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (2:1:4-3:0:7)
      para (2:3:6-3:0:7)
        str (2:3:6-2:3:6) text="a"
````

Block quotes inside a list item carry positions; a blank line ends the first.
```` ap
- a

  > q

  para
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-6:0:18) tight=false style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-6:0:18)
      para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
        str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
      block_quote (3:3:7-5:0:11)
        para (3:5:9-4:0:10)
          str (3:5:9-3:5:9) text="q"
      para (5:3:14-6:0:18)
        str (5:3:14-5:6:17) text="para"
````

A sublist followed directly by a block quote: both positioned.
```` ap
- a

  - b
  > q
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-5:0:16) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-5:0:16)
