````

An unclosed delimiter is text, in one `str` with what follows.
```` ap
_a b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:4)
    str (1:1:0-1:4:3) text="_a b"
````

Two delimiters with nothing between them are text.
```` ap
__
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:2)
    str (1:1:0-1:2:1) text="__"
````

A delimiter that can neither open nor close is text.
```` ap
a * b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:5:4) text="a * b"
````

A link spans from its bracket to its closing parenthesis.
```` ap
a [t](u) b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:10)
    str (1:1:0-1:2:1) text="a "
    link (1:3:2-1:8:7) destination="u"
      str (1:4:3-1:4:3) text="t"
    str (1:9:8-1:10:9) text=" b"
````

Attributes after a link do not extend it.
```` ap
[t](u){.c}
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:10)
    link (1:1:0-1:6:5) destination="u" class="c"
      str (1:2:1-1:2:1) text="t"
````

A link whose text crosses a line; the soft break sits on the newline.
```` ap
[a
b](u)
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-3:0:8)
    link (1:1:0-2:5:7) destination="u"
      str (1:2:1-1:2:1) text="a"
      soft_break (2:0:2-2:0:2)
      str (2:1:3-2:1:3) text="b"
````

A link whose destination crosses a line ends on the closing parenthesis.
```` ap
[t](u
  v)
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-3:0:10)
    link (1:1:0-2:4:9) destination="uv"
      str (1:2:1-1:2:1) text="t"
````

A bracket without a closing one is text, merged with what follows.
```` ap
[a](b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:5:4) text="[a](b"
````

An image starts on its bracket, as djot.js (the `!` is left out).
```` ap
![alt](u) b
.
