    str (2:1:3-2:1:3) text="b"
````

A hard break after trailing spaces sits on the newline.
```` ap
a  \
b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-3:0:6)
    str (1:1:0-1:1:0) text="a"
    hard_break (2:0:4-2:0:4)
    str (2:1:5-2:1:5) text="b"
````

A soft break sits on the newline it replaces.
```` ap
a
b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-3:0:3)
    str (1:1:0-1:1:0) text="a"
    soft_break (2:0:1-2:0:1)
    str (2:1:2-2:1:2) text="b"
````

Positions across three lines, with emphasis crossing a line.
```` ap
one
two _e
m_ three
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-4:0:19)
    str (1:1:0-1:3:2) text="one"
    soft_break (2:0:3-2:0:3)
    str (2:1:4-2:4:7) text="two "
    emph (2:5:8-3:2:12)
      str (2:6:9-2:6:9) text="e"
      soft_break (3:0:10-3:0:10)
      str (3:1:11-3:1:11) text="m"
    str (3:3:13-3:8:18) text=" three"
````

An escaped character starts the text after the backslash.
```` ap
a \* b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:6)
    str (1:1:0-1:2:1) text="a "
    str (1:4:3-1:6:5) text="* b"
````

An escaped backslash.
```` ap
a \\ b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:6)
    str (1:1:0-1:2:1) text="a "
    str (1:4:3-1:6:5) text="\\ b"
````

A backslash before a tab is text.
```` ap
a\	b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:4)
    str (1:1:0-1:4:3) text="a\\\tb"
````

A non-breaking space sits on the escaped space.
```` ap
a\ b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:4)
    str (1:1:0-1:1:0) text="a"
    non_breaking_space (1:3:2-1:3:2)
    str (1:4:3-1:4:3) text="b"
````

Attributes on emphasis do not extend its span.
```` ap
_em_{.c} after
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:14)
    emph (1:1:0-1:4:3) class="c"
      str (1:2:1-1:3:2) text="em"
    str (1:9:8-1:14:13) text=" after"
````

An unmatched opening bracket is text, in one `str`.
```` ap
a [ b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:5:4) text="a [ b"
````

An unmatched `![` is text.
```` ap
a ![ b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:6)
    str (1:1:0-1:6:5) text="a ![ b"
````

An unmatched closing bracket is text.
```` ap
a ] b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:5:4) text="a ] b"
````

A brace that opens no attribute is text.
```` ap
a { b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:5:4) text="a { b"
````

An unclosed attribute is text.
```` ap
a{.c b
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:6)
    str (1:1:0-1:6:5) text="a{.c b"
````

A paragraph starts at its first non-space character.
```` ap
  a
.
doc
  para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
    str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
````

A paragraph ends one past its last non-blank character when whitespace trails it.
```` ap
a   b  
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-1:6:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:5:4) text="a   b"
````

Trailing spaces on a continuation line stay in the text; the paragraph ends one past its content.
```` ap
a  
b  
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:2:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:3:2) text="a  "
    soft_break (2:0:3-2:0:3)
    str (2:1:4-2:1:4) text="b"
````

A list item's paragraph ends one past its content when whitespace trails it; the list ends at the input's end.
```` ap
- a  
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-2:0:5) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-2:0:5)
      para (1:3:2-1:4:3)
        str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
````

A block quote's paragraph ends one past its content when whitespace trails it.
```` ap
> q  
.
doc
  block_quote (1:1:0-2:0:5)
    para (1:3:2-1:4:3)
      str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="q"
````

An indented continuation line with trailing spaces.
```` ap
a
  b  
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:4:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:1:0) text="a"
    soft_break (2:0:1-2:0:1)
    str (2:3:4-2:3:4) text="b"
````

An unclosed code block runs to the end of the input, blank lines included.
```` ap
```
x

.
doc
  code_block (1:1:0-4:0:6) text="x\n\n"
````

A list followed by blank lines ends at the end of the input.
```` ap
- a


.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-4:0:5) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-4:0:5)
      para (1:3:2-2:0:3)
        str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
````

A heading inside a block quote: its inlines carry positions and a soft break sits on the newline.
```` ap
