A reference definition line ends a heading.
````
# A
[r]: u

[r]
.
<section id="A">
<h1>A</h1>
<p>[r]</p>
</section>
````

A footnote definition line ends a heading.
````
# A
[^n]: note

x[^n]
.
<section id="A">
<h1>A</h1>
<p>x<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
</section>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>note<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````

A reference definition without a value on its line ends a heading.
````
# A
[r]:
  u
.
<section id="A">
<h1>A</h1>
</section>
````

A definition line does not interrupt a paragraph.
````
para
[r]: u
.
<p>para
[r]: u</p>
````

Rows without a closing pipe are a paragraph, as djot.js.
````
| a | b
|---|---
| 1 | 2
.
<p>| a | b
|—|—
| 1 | 2</p>
````

A separator row without a closing pipe ends the table; the rows above have no header.
````
| a | b |
|---|---
| 1 | 2 |
.
<table>
<tr>
<td>a</td>
<td>b</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>|—|—
| 1 | 2 |</p>
````

A second row without a closing pipe is a paragraph.
````
| a |
| b
.
<table>
<tr>
<td>a</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>| b</p>
````

