````

A backslash ending a paragraph renders `<br>`.
````
a\
.
<p>a<br>
</p>
````

A backslash ending a heading renders `<br>`.
````
# h\
.
<section id="h">
<h1>h<br>
</h1>
</section>
````

A bare checkbox opens no paragraph: the next unindented line is a new paragraph.
```` ap
- [ ]
foo
.
doc
  task_list (1:1:0-2:1:6)
    task_list_item (1:1:0-2:0:5) checked=false
  para (2:1:6-3:0:9)
    str (2:1:6-2:3:8) text="foo"
````

A bare checkbox with trailing spaces opens no paragraph either.
```` ap
- [ ]  
foo
.
doc
  task_list (1:1:0-2:1:8)
    task_list_item (1:1:0-2:0:7) checked=false
  para (2:1:8-3:0:11)
    str (2:1:8-2:3:10) text="foo"
````

An empty caption marker line followed by text: the caption starts on the marker's newline and holds the text.
```` ap
| a |
|---|
^ 
more
.
doc
  table (1:1:0-4:0:14)
    caption (4:0:14-5:0:19)
      str (4:1:15-4:4:18) text="more"
    row (1:1:0-2:0:5) head=true
      cell (1:1:0-1:5:4) head=true align="default"
        str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
````

A bare checkbox followed by a line of text renders an empty task item and a paragraph.
````
- [ ]
foo
.
<ul class="task-list">
<li>
<input disabled="" type="checkbox"/>
</li>
</ul>
<p>foo</p>
````

A heading whose text is a link gets its id from the link text.
````
# [x](u)
.
<section id="x">
<h1><a href="u">x</a></h1>
</section>
````

A heading whose text is verbatim gets its id from the verbatim text.
````
# `code`
.
<section id="code">
<h1><code>code</code></h1>
</section>
````

A heading whose text is emphasised gets its id from the emphasised text.
````
# _only_
.
<section id="only">
<h1><em>only</em></h1>
</section>
````

An implicit reference to a heading with inline formatting resolves.
````
# a _b_ c

See [a b c][]
.
<section id="a-b-c">
<h1>a <em>b</em> c</h1>
<p>See <a href="#a-b-c">a b c</a></p>
</section>
````

Heading ids take verbatim and math text.
````
# `code` and $`m` [l](u)
.
<section id="code-and-m-l">
<h1><code>code</code> and <span class="math inline">\(m\)</span> <a href="u">l</a></h1>
</section>
````

A hard break in a heading counts as whitespace for its id and implicit reference.
````
# a\
b

[a b][]
.
<section id="a-b">
<h1>a<br>
b</h1>
<p><a href="#a-b">a b</a></p>
</section>
````

An implicit reference to a heading with strong emphasis.
````
# Hi *there*

[Hi there][]
.
<section id="Hi-there">
<h1>Hi <strong>there</strong></h1>
<p><a href="#Hi-there">Hi there</a></p>
</section>
````

A reference label from verbatim link text.
````
[`x`][]

[x]: u
.
<p><a href="u"><code>x</code></a></p>
````

An implicit reference must match the heading text exactly: `[FOO][]` to `# Foo` stays unresolved.
````
# Foo

See [Foo][] and [FOO][]
.
<section id="Foo">
<h1>Foo</h1>
<p>See <a href="#Foo">Foo</a> and <a>FOO</a></p>
</section>
````

A block attribute that opens but cannot close is text, as djot.js reparses it.
````
{.a
.b}
para
.
<p>{.a
.b}
para</p>
````

A failed multi-line block attribute followed by text on its closing line.
````
{.a
.b} y
.
<p>{.a
.b} y</p>
````

A failed block attribute after one that applied.
````
{.a .b}
{.c
.d}
para
.
<p class="a b">{.c
.d}
para</p>
````

A failed block attribute alone in a paragraph.
````
{.a
.b}

para
.
<p>{.a
.b}</p>
<p>para</p>
````

An indented failed block attribute.
````
  {.a
  .b}
para
.
<p>{.a
.b}
para</p>
````

An inline attribute with nothing before it applies to nothing.
````
{.a} word
.
<p> word</p>
````

A failed block attribute after a paragraph line is an inline attribute, dropped.
````
word
{.a
.b}
.
<p>word
</p>
````

Attributes on emphasis render.
````
_e_{.a}
.
<p><em class="a">e</em></p>
````

Attributes on strong emphasis render.
````
*s*{.a}
.
<p><strong class="a">s</strong></p>
````

Attributes on verbatim render.
````
`v`{.a}
.
<p><code class="a">v</code></p>
````

Attributes on superscript render.
````
^s^{.a}
.
<p><sup class="a">s</sup></p>
````

Attributes on subscript render.
````
~s~{.a}
.
<p><sub class="a">s</sub></p>
````

Attributes on insert render.
````
{+i+}{.a}
.
<p><ins class="a">i</ins></p>
````

Attributes on delete render.
````
{-d-}{.a}
.
<p><del class="a">d</del></p>
````

Attributes on mark render.
````
{=m=}{.a}
.
<p><mark class="a">m</mark></p>
````

Attributes on an image follow its src.
````
![i](u){.a}
.
<p><img alt="i" src="u" class="a"></p>
````

Attributes on an autolink follow its href.
````
<http://x>{.a}
.
<p><a href="http://x" class="a">http://x</a></p>
````

Attributes on an email autolink.
````
<a@b.c>{.a}
.
<p><a href="mailto:a@b.c" class="a">a@b.c</a></p>
````

A class on inline math joins the intrinsic class.
````
$`m`{.a}
.
<p><span class="math inline a">\(m\)</span></p>
````

A class on display math joins the intrinsic class.
````
$$`m`{.a}
.
<p><span class="math display a">\[m\]</span></p>
````

Id and other attributes on math follow the class.
````
$`m`{#i .a k=v}
.
<p><span class="math inline a" id="i" k="v">\(m\)</span></p>
````

Attributes on emphasis keep their source order.
````
_e_{#i .a k=v}
.
<p><em id="i" class="a" k="v">e</em></p>
````

Attributes on an image keep their source order.
````
![i](u){#i k=v .a}
.
<p><img alt="i" src="u" id="i" k="v" class="a"></p>
````

Id, class and key on verbatim.
````
`v`{#i .a k=v}
.
<p><code id="i" class="a" k="v">v</code></p>
````

Id, class and key on a link.
````
[l](u){#i .a k=v}
.
<p><a href="u" id="i" class="a" k="v">l</a></p>
````

Id and key on an autolink.
````
<http://x>{#i k=v}
.
<p><a href="http://x" id="i" k="v">http://x</a></p>
````

A class on a footnote reference follows its role.
````
x[^n]{.a}

[^n]: n
.
<p>x<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref" class="a"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>n<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````


Inline ids: pass one sees them wherever they sit, as djot.js.

An inline id claims its id before a later heading.
````
[x]{#Foo}

# Foo

[Foo][]
.
<p><span id="Foo">x</span></p>
<section id="Foo-1">
<h1>Foo</h1>
<p><a href="#Foo-1">Foo</a></p>
</section>
````

An inline id in a table cell claims its id before a later heading.
````
| [x]{#Foo} |
|---|

# Foo
.
<table>
<tr>
<th><span id="Foo">x</span></th>
</tr>
</table>
<section id="Foo-1">
<h1>Foo</h1>
</section>
````

Inline ids inside a list item and a block quote claim their ids before later headings.
````
- [x]{#Foo}

# Foo

> [y]{#Bar}

# Bar
.
<ul>
<li>
<span id="Foo">x</span>
</li>
</ul>
<section id="Foo-1">
<h1>Foo</h1>
<blockquote>
<p><span id="Bar">y</span></p>
</blockquote>
</section>
<section id="Bar-1">
<h1>Bar</h1>
</section>
````


Footnotes: references by label, definitions after the document, endnotes numbered by first use.

A footnote referencing another footnote; each definition ends where the next block starts.
```` ap
a[^x]

[^x]: see[^y]

[^y]: y
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:5)
    str (1:1:0-1:1:0) text="a"
    footnote_reference (1:2:1-1:5:4) text="x"
  footnote (3:1:7-5:1:22) label="x"
    para (3:7:13-4:0:20)
      str (3:7:13-3:9:15) text="see"
      footnote_reference (3:10:16-3:13:19) text="y"
  footnote (5:1:22-6:0:29) label="y"
    para (5:7:28-6:0:29)
      str (5:7:28-5:7:28) text="y"
````

A reference to no definition, and a definition nothing references; two paragraphs after a blank.
```` ap
test[^nonexistent]

[^unused]: note

  more
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:18)
    str (1:1:0-1:4:3) text="test"
    footnote_reference (1:5:4-1:18:17) text="nonexistent"
  footnote (3:1:20-6:0:43) label="unused"
    para (3:12:31-4:0:35)
      str (3:12:31-3:15:34) text="note"
    para (5:3:39-6:0:43)
      str (5:3:39-5:6:42) text="more"
````

A definition with a lazy line, a sublist, a block quote and a second definition.
```` ap
See[^a] and[^b].

[^a]: First para
  lazy line

  - item one
  - item two

  > quoted

[^b]: Short
.
doc
  para (1:1:0-2:0:16)
    str (1:1:0-1:3:2) text="See"
    footnote_reference (1:4:3-1:7:6) text="a"
    str (1:8:7-1:11:10) text=" and"
    footnote_reference (1:12:11-1:15:14) text="b"
    str (1:16:15-1:16:15) text="."
  footnote (3:1:18-11:1:87) label="a"
    para (3:7:24-5:0:46)
      str (3:7:24-3:16:33) text="First para"
      soft_break (4:0:34-4:0:34)
      str (4:3:37-4:11:45) text="lazy line"
    bullet_list (6:3:50-9:3:77) tight=true style="-"
      list_item (6:3:50-7:2:62)
        para (6:5:52-7:0:60)
          str (6:5:52-6:12:59) text="item one"
      list_item (7:3:63-9:2:76)
        para (7:5:65-8:0:73)
          str (7:5:65-7:12:72) text="item two"
    block_quote (9:3:77-11:0:86)
      para (9:5:79-10:0:85)
        str (9:5:79-9:10:84) text="quoted"
  footnote (11:1:87-12:0:98) label="b"
    para (11:7:93-12:0:98)
      str (11:7:93-11:11:97) text="Short"
````

A definition inside a block quote ends with the quote.
```` ap
> a[^x]
>
> [^x]: in quote

para
.
doc
  block_quote (1:1:0-5:0:27)
    para (1:3:2-2:0:7)
      str (1:3:2-1:3:2) text="a"
      footnote_reference (1:4:3-1:7:6) text="x"
  para (5:1:28-6:0:32)
    str (5:1:28-5:4:31) text="para"
  footnote (3:3:12-5:0:27) label="x"
    para (3:9:18-4:0:26)
      str (3:9:18-3:16:25) text="in quote"
````

A footnote referenced only from another footnote is numbered when that endnote is written.
````
a[^x]

[^x]: see[^y]

[^y]: y
.
<p>a<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>see<a id="fnref2" href="#fn2" role="doc-noteref"><sup>2</sup></a><a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
<li id="fn2">
<p>y<a href="#fnref2" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````


Fenced divs: the first fitting fence closes the outermost div, indented or not; only a code block holds a fence line.

A closing fence of the same length closes the outer div; the inner closes with it, and the rest is a paragraph.
````
::: a
::: b
x
:::
y
:::
.
<div class="a">
<div class="b">
<p>x</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>y
:::</p>
````

An indented closing fence inside a list item closes the div.
````
::: a
- x
  :::
y
:::
.
<div class="a">
<ul>
<li>
x
</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p>y
:::</p>
````

An indented closing fence right after the opener closes the div.
````
::: a
  :::
z
.
<div class="a">
</div>
<p>z</p>
````

A code fence after an item's paragraph is text, so the fence line inside it closes the div.
````
::: a
- x
  ```
  :::
  ```
:::
.
<div class="a">
<ul>
<li>
x
<code></code>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
<pre><code>:::
</code></pre>
````

A code block inside a nested div holds its fence line; the next fence closes the outer div.
````
::: a
::: b
```
:::
```
w
:::
z
:::
.
<div class="a">
<div class="b">
<pre><code>:::
</code></pre>
<p>w</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>z
:::</p>
````

Nested divs with equal fences: the outer ends on the fence, the inner past it.
```` ap
::: a
::: b
x
:::
.
doc
  div (1:1:0-4:3:16) class="a"
    div (2:1:6-5:0:17) class="b"
      para (3:1:12-4:0:13)
        str (3:1:12-3:1:12) text="x"
````

A div unclosed inside an item ends where the item's list ends; the fence opens a new div.
```` ap
- ::: a
  x
:::
.
doc
  bullet_list (1:1:0-3:1:12) tight=true style="-"
    list_item (1:1:0-3:0:11)
      div (1:3:2-3:1:12) class="a"
        para (2:3:10-3:0:11)
          str (2:3:10-2:3:10) text="x"
  div (3:1:12-4:0:15)
````

A list closed by the fence ends past it.
```` ap
::: a
- x
- y
:::
para
.
doc
  div (1:1:0-4:3:16) class="a"
    bullet_list (2:1:6-5:0:17) tight=true style="-"
      list_item (2:1:6-3:0:9)
        para (2:3:8-3:0:9)
          str (2:3:8-2:3:8) text="x"
      list_item (3:1:10-4:3:16)
        para (3:3:12-4:0:13)
          str (3:3:12-3:3:12) text="y"
  para (5:1:18-6:0:22)
    str (5:1:18-5:4:21) text="para"
````


Review fixes after the window rewrite.

A footnote defined twice: the later definition replaces the earlier, and its headings get their ids where it stands.
````
a[^x]

[^x]: first

b

[^x]: ## H

c
.
<p>a<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
<p>b</p>
<p>c</p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<h2 id="H">H</h2>
<p><a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````

A footnote defined twice without a block between: the later wins.
````
a[^x]

[^x]: first

[^x]: second
.
<p>a<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>second<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````

A tab-indented closing fence closes the div.
````
::: a
x
	:::
y
.
<div class="a">
<p>x</p>
</div>
<p>y</p>
````

The div closed by a tab-indented fence ends after its colons.
```` ap
::: a
x
	:::
y
.
doc
  div (1:1:0-3:4:11) class="a"
    para (2:1:6-3:0:7)
      str (2:1:6-2:1:6) text="x"
  para (4:1:13-5:0:14)
    str (4:1:13-4:1:13) text="y"
````


One class, one start: a block attribute joins a div's class; an ordered list keeps its start and type under attributes.

A block attribute's class joins the div's own.
````
{.x}
::: y
z
:::
.
<div class="x y">
<p>z</p>
</div>
````

A block attribute keeps an ordered list's start.
````
{.x}
2. a
.
<ol start="2" class="x">
<li>
a
</li>
</ol>
````

A block attribute keeps an ordered list's type; the list's own come first.
````
{#i .x k=v}
i. a
.
<ol type="i" id="i" class="x" k="v">
<li>
a
</li>
</ol>
````

Roman and alpha markers: the AST prints no type.
```` ap
i. a
ii. b
c. d
.
doc
  ordered_list (1:1:0-4:0:15) tight=true
    list_item (1:1:0-2:0:4)
      para (1:4:3-2:0:4)
        str (1:4:3-1:4:3) text="a"
    list_item (2:1:5-3:0:10)
      para (2:5:9-3:0:10)
        str (2:5:9-2:5:9) text="b"
    list_item (3:1:11-4:0:15)
      para (3:4:14-4:0:15)
        str (3:4:14-3:4:14) text="d"
````

Parenthesised alpha markers and a start of 5: the AST prints no start.
```` ap
(a) x
(b) y

5) z
.
doc
  ordered_list (1:1:0-4:1:13) tight=true
    list_item (1:1:0-2:0:5)
      para (1:5:4-2:0:5)
        str (1:5:4-1:5:4) text="x"
    list_item (2:1:6-4:0:12)
      para (2:5:10-3:0:11)
        str (2:5:10-2:5:10) text="y"
  ordered_list (4:1:13-5:0:17) tight=true
    list_item (4:1:13-5:0:17)
      para (4:4:16-5:0:17)
        str (4:4:16-4:4:16) text="z"
````

A block attribute with an id and a key before a div with a class: id, class, key.
```` ap
{#i k=v}
::: y
z
:::
.
doc
  div (2:1:9-4:3:19) id="i" class="y" k="v"
    para (3:1:15-4:0:16)
      str (3:1:15-3:1:15) text="z"
````


Sections end at the document's last block event, as djot.js: the last block's end, or the input's end after trailing blank lines or a div.

A last heading with trailing whitespace ends its section one past its text.
```` ap
{#h}
# H  
.
doc
  section (2:1:5-2:4:8) id="h"
    heading (2:1:5-2:4:8) level=1
      str (2:3:7-2:3:7) text="H"
````

A code block closed on the last line ends the section on its fence.
```` ap
{#a}
# A
```
x
```  
.
doc
  section (2:1:5-5:3:17) id="a"
    heading (2:1:5-3:0:8) level=1
      str (2:3:7-2:3:7) text="A"
    code_block (3:1:9-5:3:17) text="x\n"
````

Nested sections both end at the last paragraph's content.
```` ap
{#a}
# A
{#b}
## B
text  
.
doc
  section (2:1:5-5:5:23) id="a"
    heading (2:1:5-3:0:8) level=1
      str (2:3:7-2:3:7) text="A"
    section (4:1:14-5:5:23) id="b"
      heading (4:1:14-5:5:23) level=2
        str (4:4:17-4:4:17) text="B"
        soft_break (5:0:18-5:0:18)
        str (5:1:19-5:4:22) text="text"
````

A div last: the section ends at the input's end.
```` ap
{#h}
# H
::: d
x
:::
.
doc
  section (2:1:5-6:0:20) id="h"
    heading (2:1:5-3:0:8) level=1
      str (2:3:7-2:3:7) text="H"
    div (3:1:9-5:3:19) class="d"
      para (4:1:15-5:0:16)
        str (4:1:15-4:1:15) text="x"
````

Trailing blank lines: the section ends at the input's end.
```` ap
{#h}
# H

para

.
doc
  section (2:1:5-6:0:15) id="h"
    heading (2:1:5-3:0:8) level=1
      str (2:3:7-2:3:7) text="H"
    para (4:1:10-5:0:14)
      str (4:1:10-4:4:13) text="para"
````
